  "body": "## What changed\n\n`crates/sim/src/verify/rapids.rs`: a sideways rapid under the clearance plane is judged along its whole length, not only at its start, mid and end. Each station uses #106's footprint test (8 rings at d·k/8, each judged at the inner ring's tip lift).\n\n- Step: d/8 (the ring spacing; d = r − gouge_tol), floored at 0.01 mm; stations = ceil(len/step), both ends included. The footprint reaches d ahead of and behind each station, so no wall can slip between stations. What's left is the footprint's own sampling bound from #106, which the module doc states.\n- It runs whether or not there's a model, since it's independent of `hidden_along`'s early return.\n- Cost: 73 samples per station. A rapid that would need more than 2^18 stations (about 98 m for a 6 mm tool) is refused as RapidInStock, not checked coarser, and the doc says so.\n\n## Pins (`crates/sim/tests/sideways_rapids.rs`)\n\n- `a_floor_link_through_a_4mm_wall_between_two_pockets_is_a_rapid_in_stock` (the issue's scenario): fails on main\n- `a_floor_link_through_a_1mm_wall_is_a_rapid_in_stock`: fails on main\n- `a_long_floor_link_over_a_fully_cut_slot_is_clean`: no warnings at all, guarding against false refusals\n\n## Readings\n\nGreen: sim lib 54, vertical_rapids 16, radial_rapids 15, sideways_rapids 3; motion finish3d 55, flow 13, pivot5d 7 (no real link rapid refused); app center_cut_multiaxis 6, verify 21, golden_cl 23, posting 17, vertical_rapid_stock 4; no golden changed; clippy on sim and app is clean.\n\nNote: main is red on 7 lathe tests since PR #138 (#159: the footprint law judging turning rapids). That's fixed in PR #135. The turning suites will be re-run on this branch once #135 lands.\n\nChangelog: Sideways rapids under the clearance plane are judged along their whole length, so a link rapid through a narrow uncut wall between two pockets is refused instead of posted\n\nFixes #140\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
